{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>It shall be whole.</b> For if one were to take a handful from it with three fingers, as with the other meal-offerings, what gift would there be in that before HaShem? And what would it matter if he made all his foods into meal-offerings? It is not comparable to all the meal-offerings of Israel, for there the handful is burned and the remainder is eaten by the priests, who are the ministers of HaShem — thus the entire thing is a gift. Nor is it comparable to the sin-offering and guilt-offering of priests, for there the fats are burned and the skin goes to the men of the watch. So too here, the proper ruling is that it be burned, since it is his meal-offering, as we find with the two bulls of his that he offered during the eight days of inauguration, which were burned even though they were outer sin-offerings."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:10:18.207449482Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}